ar em conta?"]}]},{"tag":"Verbos","title":"Verbs in focus","blocks":[{"type":"verbs","items":[{"v":"rest","pt":"descansar","forms":[["I / you / we / they rest","Rest after work."],["he / she / it rests","Descanse após o trabalho."]]}]},{"type":"table","head":["Phrasal verb","Significado","Exemplo"],"rows":[["**take into account**","levar em conta","Take the cost into account. — Leve o custo em conta."]],"cap":"Phrasal verbs"}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"Poetry circle","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"Poetry circle","lines":[["Ana","What is the speaker supposed to do?","O que o falante deve fazer?"],["Leo","Smile and say the right thing.","Sorrir e dizer a coisa certa."],["Ana","What should we take into account?","O que devemos levar em conta?"],["Leo","The hours the speaker has been giving.","As horas que o falante tem dedicado."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: Ligações e assimilação","items":[{"label":"Ligações e assimilação","note":"Sons se ligam e se transformam: did you → didja; want you → wanchu; pick it up → pi-ki-dup.","words":["did you","want you","pick it up","last night","what you"]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Say what is expected.","pt":"Diga.","model":"I’m supposed to smile."},{"q":"Say what you’re not supposed to do.","pt":"Diga.","model":"I’m not supposed to cry."},{"q":"Use take into account.","pt":"Use.","model":"Take the traffic into account."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write 5 sentences about expectations at work or school using be supposed to and take into account.","model":"I’m supposed to answer emails quickly. We aren’t supposed to eat at our desks. Tom was supposed to finish the report yesterday. Please take the workload into account. What am I supposed to do now?","checklist":["Usei **be supposed to**","Usei **take into account**","5 frases"],"words":"5 frases"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · E